+## AGC 26.2 alpha15 - high-scale survival optimisation plane
+
+Alpha15 focuses on the first wave of important thousand-player survival optimisations before small tuning:
+
+- `AGCScaleControlPlane`: one central budget for packet-shape reuse, cohorts, chunk-intent compaction, entity banding, plugin translation and memory-local scratch work.
+- `AGCPacketShapeTable`: tick-local packet shape reuse. It never shares mutable packet instances, never drops packets and never reorders a connection stream.
+- `AGCPlayerCohortTable`: coarse player cohorts for shared read-only fanout planning. Cohorts are planning labels only; they do not hide players or reduce view distance.
+- `AGCChunkIntentCompactor`: region-shaped chunk intent planning while preserving Paper chunk queue FIFO and completion order.
+- `AGCEntityBandingPlanner`: read-only entity tracker candidate bands. Entity tick, AI, damage and interaction logic remain untouched.
+- `AGCMemoryLocalityPlanner`: tick-local scratch budgeting to reduce allocation churn without retaining live world state.
+- `AGCEncodingReusePlanner`: immutable encoding helper planning before ordered connection writes; protocol-sensitive packets keep ordered encoding.
+- `AGCPluginBackpressureBridge`: routes plugin helper work through read-only prepare or ordered primary-thread commit and rejects off-thread Bukkit mutation.
+- `AGCHotspotEvictionPlanner`: evicts only duplicate read-only helper plans under hotspot pressure; it never unloads chunks, hides entities or drops packets.
+
+Operator report: `/agc scale15`.
+
+Hard rules remain: no packet drops, no chunk FIFO head skip, no entity tick/AI/damage/interaction skip, no Bukkit off-thread mutation, no plugin event reorder and no redstone/factory semantics changes.
